96	 * Fixed ONCE — before any money moves — and carried to the moment it is charged.
97	 *
98	 * REAL INCIDENT (2026-07-26 customer-journey rehearsal, H2). The card-paid deploy
99	 * path quoted a total, charged the CARD its share of that total at Stripe, and
100	 * then — on the confirm redirect, minutes or hours later — re-ran `orderQuote`
101	 * and debited whatever came back. That re-run includes `currentPromo(new Date())`,
102	 * and lib/promotions.ts always has an active sale that rotates by calendar date,
103	 * so a rotation between "customer clicked Deploy" and "customer came back from
104	 * Stripe" re-priced the order AFTER the card had cleared and took the difference
105	 * out of the wallet with no new consent. With no balance to take it from, the
106	 * payment was captured and no server was created.
107	 *
108	 * `lib/resize.ts` and `lib/disk-expand.ts` already carried the amount through
109	 * Stripe metadata for exactly this reason; the order path was the one that
110	 * re-derived it. Same rule as lib/renewal-quote.ts and lib/proration.ts: a figure
111	 * the customer was shown is not recomputed later, it is carried.
112	 *
113	 * `promoPercent` and `promoName` travel WITH the total because they are not
114	 * decoration. `Server.termPromoPercent` records the rate a term was actually sold
115	 * at (every later proration prices against it), and the promo name is the ledger
116	 * and invoice text the customer reads. Honouring a 30%-off price while stamping
117	 * today's 15% would hand every later proration the wrong basis and print a
118	 * discount on the invoice that does not match the money taken.
119	 */
120	export type OrderPrice = {
121	  /**
122	   * The NET (pre-tax) total the customer consented to, in cents. Its meaning is
123	   * unchanged by Finding 1 — every promo/coupon/proration figure is computed against
124	   * this net. The amount actually CHARGED is `chargeCents + (taxCents ?? 0)`.
125	   */
126	  chargeCents: number;
127	  /** Promo rate (%) that produced it; persisted as `Server.termPromoPercent`. */
128	  promoPercent: number;
129	  /** Promo name for the ledger / invoice line, e.g. "Summer Sale". */
130	  promoName: string;
131	  /**
132	   * VAT/GST on the net (Finding 1), carried through the card round-trip so the
133	   * confirm route settles the SAME tax-inclusive total the card leg was split from
134	   * — never re-derived after the card cleared. Absent on legacy/full-price sessions,
135	   * in which case the charge path recomputes it from the owner's country (0 by
136	   * default), which can only ever undertax, the conservative direction.
137	   */
138	  taxCents?: number;
139	  taxRatePercent?: number;
140	  taxCountry?: string;
